/-!
# Sheaves on an fppf hypercovering of an algebraic space

Let `S` be a scheme, `X` an algebraic space over `S`, `U` a simplicial algebraic space over `S`
and `a : U → X` an augmentation which is an fppf hypercovering of `X` (Section 0DH4), with the
morphism of topoi `a : Sh(U_étale) → Sh(X_étale)` of Section 0DE7. This file proves the content of
Stacks 0DH6: `a⁻¹ : Sh(X_étale) ⥤ Sh(U_étale)` and `a⁻¹ : Ab(X_étale) ⥤ Ab(U_étale)` are fully
faithful with essential image the cartesian sheaves and quasi-inverse `a_*`.

## The proof

This is the proof of the source. In the commutative square of topoi of Stacks 0DH5
```
Sh((Spaces/U)_{fppf, total}) --h--> Sh(U_étale)
        | a_fppf                       | a
Sh((Spaces/X)_fppf)        --h₋₁--> Sh(X_étale)
```
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.phComparisonSquareInverseImageIso` for the fppf topology), `h₋₁⁻¹` and,
through its description in each simplicial degree (Stacks 0D96), `h⁻¹` are fully faithful by
Stacks 0DGF, and `a_fppf⁻¹` is fully faithful with essential image the cartesian sheaves by
Stacks 0DA8, `U` being a hypercovering of `X` in `(Spaces/S)_fppf`. Hence `a⁻¹` is fully faithful.

For a cartesian sheaf `G` on `U_étale` the sheaf `h⁻¹G` is cartesian, so `h⁻¹G = a_fppf⁻¹ℋ` for a
sheaf `ℋ` on `(Spaces/X)_fppf`. Restricted to the degree `0` this reads
`h_{U_0}⁻¹G_0 = (a_{0, big})⁻¹ℋ`; as `a_0 : U_0 → X` is flat, locally of finite presentation and
surjective, `ℋ = h₋₁⁻¹ℱ` for a sheaf `ℱ` on `X_étale` by Stacks 0DGL. Then
`h⁻¹a⁻¹ℱ = a_fppf⁻¹h₋₁⁻¹ℱ = h⁻¹G`, and `a⁻¹ℱ = G` by full faithfulness of `h⁻¹`. The statements on
abelian sheaves follow, the units and counits of the abelian adjunction forgetting to those of the
adjunction on sheaves of sets.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.mem_essImage_fppfComparison_of_overMap`: Stacks 0DGL for the
  inclusions `X_{spaces, étale} → (Spaces/X)_fppf`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFppfHypercovering.etaleAugmentation_inverseImage_fullyFaithful`:
  the content of Stacks 0DH6, sheaves of sets.
* `Space.IsFppfHypercovering.etaleAugmentation_abelianInverseImage_fullyFaithful`: the content
  of Stacks 0DH6, sheaves of abelian groups.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFppfHypercovering.mem_essImage_totalInverseImageAb`: every cartesian
  abelian sheaf on `U_étale` is `a⁻¹` of an abelian sheaf on `X_étale`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.EtaleComponent.smallEtale_inverseImage_fullyFaithful` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.EtaleComponent.smallEtale_abelianInverseImage_fullyFaithful`:
  Stacks 0DH6 on the small étale site of `X`, for sheaves of sets and of abelian groups.

## Implementation notes

`X = A.right`, `U = A.left` and `a = A.hom`; `X_étale` is the spaces-étale site of `X`, which
Section 0DE7 identifies with the small étale site. The fppf site of algebraic spaces is the one
whose topology is generated by all fppf coverings (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.fppfTopology`).
Stacks 0DGL is available for a big fppf site of algebraic spaces in the sense of Stacks 0DBV,
whose topology is the fppf topology
(`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSpaceSite.topology_eq_spaceFppfTopology`); it is carried along that
equality. "Quasi-inverse `a_*`" is the invertibility of the unit of `a⁻¹ ⊣ a_*` and of its counit
at the cartesian sheaves.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DH6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DH6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DH5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DH5)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DGF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DGF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DGL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DGL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DA8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DA8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D96](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D96)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Simplicial

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSpaceSite

open Space

variable {S : Scheme.{u}} (T : BigFppfSpaceSite S)

/-- **The inclusion `X_{spaces, étale} → (Spaces/X)_fppf` is continuous** for the topology of a
big fppf site of algebraic spaces: an étale covering is an fppf covering (Stacks 0DFC). -/
instance spacesEtale_inclusion_isContinuous (X : T.Spaces) :
    (SpacesEtale.inclusion T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem X).IsContinuous
      (SpacesEtale.topology T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem X) (BigFppfSpaceOver.topology T X) := by
  change (SpacesEtale.inclusion T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem X).IsContinuous _
    (T.topology.over X)
  rw [topology_eq_spaceFppfTopology]
  infer_instance

/-- The inverse image along `X_{spaces, étale} → (Spaces/X)_fppf` is the inverse image of the
comparison morphism `a_X` of Stacks 0DGI: the two are left adjoint to the same direct image,
restriction along `V ↦ V/X`. -/
def spacesEtaleComparisonInverseImageIso (X : T.Spaces) :
    (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism T.topology X).inverseImage ≅
      (fppfToSmallEtaleMorphism T T.bigEtaleSpaceSite rfl X).inverseImage :=
  (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism T.topology X).adj.leftAdjointUniq
    (fppfToSmallEtaleMorphism T T.bigEtaleSpaceSite rfl X).adj

/-- **Stacks 0DGL on the inclusions `X_{spaces, étale} → (Spaces/X)_fppf`**, for the topology of
`T`. Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be flat, locally of finite presentation and surjective, and `H` a big fppf
sheaf on `X` whose restriction to `Spaces/Y` along `f` lies in the essential image of `h_Y⁻¹`.
Then `H` lies in the essential image of `h_X⁻¹`. -/
theorem mem_essImage_spacesEtaleComparison_of_bigFppfInverseImage {X Y : T.Spaces} (f : Y ⟶ X)
    (hf : Space.IsFlat T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem f.hom)
    (hlfp : Space.IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem f.hom)
    (hsurj : Space.IsSurjective T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem f.hom)
    {H : Sheaf (BigFppfSpaceOver.topology T X) (Type (u + 1))}
    (hH : (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism T.topology Y).inverseImage.essImage
      ((bigFppfMorphism T f).inverseImage.obj H)) :
    (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism T.topology X).inverseImage.essImage H := by
  obtain ⟨K, ⟨e⟩⟩ := hH
  obtain ⟨G, ⟨e'⟩⟩ := fppfToSmallEtale_essImage_of_bigFppfInverseImage T T.bigEtaleSpaceSite rfl
    f hf hlfp hsurj ⟨K, ⟨((spacesEtaleComparisonInverseImageIso T Y).app K).symm ≪≫ e⟩⟩
  exact ⟨G, ⟨(spacesEtaleComparisonInverseImageIso T X).app G ≪≫ e'⟩⟩

/-- **Stacks 0DGL on the inclusions `X_{spaces, étale} → Spaces/X`**, for any topology `J` on the
algebraic spaces of `T` equal to the topology of `T`, the restriction along `f` being written as
restriction along `Over.map f`. -/
theorem mem_essImage_spacesEtaleComparison_of_overMap
    (J : GrothendieckTopology T.Spaces)
    [hJc : ∀ X : T.Spaces, (SpacesEtale.inclusion T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem X).IsContinuous
      (SpacesEtale.topology T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem X) (J.over X)]
    (hJ : T.topology = J) {X Y : T.Spaces} (f : Y ⟶ X)
    (hf : Space.IsFlat T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem f.hom)
    (hlfp : Space.IsLocallyOfFinitePresentation T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem f.hom)
    (hsurj : Space.IsSurjective T.schemeSite S T.scheme_mem f.hom)
    {H : Sheaf (J.over X) (Type (u + 1))}
    (hH : (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism J Y).inverseImage.essImage
      (((Over.map f).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1)) (J.over Y) (J.over X)).obj H)) :
    (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism J X).inverseImage.essImage H := by
  subst hJ
  exact mem_essImage_spacesEtaleComparison_of_bigFppfInverseImage T f hf hlfp hsurj
    (hH.ofIso ((bigFppfMorphism_inverseImageIso T f).app H).symm)

end AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfSpaceSite

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

open Stacks.Topos.AbelianPushforward SimplicialSiteSituation.Augmentation
open Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}

/-- **Stacks 0DGL on the inclusions `X_{spaces, étale} → (Spaces/X)_fppf`.** Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a
flat, locally finitely presented, surjective morphism of algebraic spaces over `S`, and `H` a sheaf
on `(Spaces/X)_fppf` whose restriction to `(Spaces/Y)_fppf` along `f` lies in the essential image
of `h_Y⁻¹`. Then `H` lies in the essential image of `h_X⁻¹`. -/
theorem mem_essImage_fppfComparison_of_overMap {X Y : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS} (f : Y ⟶ X)
    (hf : fppfSurjective B S hS f) {H : Sheaf ((fppfTopology B S hS).over X) (Type (u + 1))}
    (hH : (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism (fppfTopology B S hS) Y).inverseImage.essImage
      (((Over.map f).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1))
        ((fppfTopology B S hS).over Y) ((fppfTopology B S hS).over X)).obj H)) :
    (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism (fppfTopology B S hS) X).inverseImage.essImage H :=
  (bigFppfSpaceSiteOfSchemeSite B S hS).mem_essImage_spacesEtaleComparison_of_overMap
    (fppfTopology B S hS) (hJc := fun X ↦ spacesEtaleInclusion_isContinuous_fppf X)
    (bigFppfSpaceSiteOfSchemeSite B S hS).topology_eq_spaceFppfTopology f hf.1 hf.2.1 hf.2.2 hH

/-- A morphism of abelian sheaves is invertible if its image in sheaves of sets is. -/
private theorem isIso_of_isIso_forget_map {C : Type (u + 1)} [Category.{u + 1} C]
    {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {F G : Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}} (f : F ⟶ G)
    (h : IsIso ((sheafCompose J (forget AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})).map f)) : IsIso f :=
  isIso_of_reflects_iso f (sheafCompose J (forget AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}))

variable {A : SimplicialObject.Augmented (AlgebraicSpaces B S hS)} (hA : IsFppfHypercovering A)
include hA

/-- **`a⁻¹ : Sh(X_étale) ⥤ Sh(U_étale)` is fully faithful** for an fppf hypercovering: through
the square of Stacks 0DH5, `h⁻¹ ∘ a⁻¹ = a_fppf⁻¹ ∘ h₋₁⁻¹` is fully faithful (Stacks 0DGF (1) and
Stacks 0DA8), and `h⁻¹` is faithful. -/
def IsFppfHypercovering.fullyFaithfulEtaleAugmentationInverseImage :
    (etaleAugmentationMorphism A).inverseImage.FullyFaithful := by
  have hX : ∀ X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS,
      IsIso (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism (fppfTopology B S hS) X).adj.unit :=
    isIso_fppfComparison_unit
  have hffh := fullyFaithfulPhComparisonInverseImage (A := A) (fppfTopology B S hS) hX
  have hffph := SimplicialOver.fullyFaithfulAugmentationInverseImage A.left A.hom
    (fppfPretopology B S hS) (isHypercoveringAugmentation_of_isFppfHypercovering hA)
    (fppfPretopology_toGrothendieck B S hS)
  haveI := hX A.right
  have hffX :=
    (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism (fppfTopology B S hS) A.right).adj.fullyFaithfulLOfIsIsoUnit
  have hcomp := (hffX.comp hffph).ofIso
    (phComparisonSquareInverseImageIso A (fppfTopology B S hS)).symm
  exact @Functor.FullyFaithful.ofCompFaithful _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ hffh.faithful hcomp

/-- **A cartesian sheaf on `U_étale` is in the essential image of `a⁻¹`**, for an fppf
hypercovering. The sheaf `h⁻¹G` is cartesian, hence `h⁻¹G ≅ a_fppf⁻¹ℋ` (Stacks 0DA8); the
restriction of `ℋ` along the fppf covering `U_0 → X` is the restriction of `h⁻¹G` to the degree
`0`, which comes from `U_{0, étale}`, so `ℋ` comes from `X_étale` by Stacks 0DGL, and `a⁻¹ℋ' = G`
by full faithfulness of `h⁻¹`. -/
theorem IsFppfHypercovering.mem_essImage_etaleAugmentation_inverseImage
    {G : Sheaf (etaleSimplicialSite A).totalTopology (Type (u + 1))}
    (hG : (etaleSituation A).IsCartesianSheaf G) :
    (etaleAugmentationMorphism A).inverseImage.essImage G := by
  have hX : ∀ X : AlgebraicSpaces B S hS,
      IsIso (spacesEtaleComparisonMorphism (fppfTopology B S hS) X).adj.unit :=
    isIso_fppfComparison_unit
  have hffh := fullyFaithfulPhComparisonInverseImage (A := A) (fppfTopology B S hS) hX
  let aph := SimplicialOver.augmentationMorphismOfTopoi (fppfTopology B S hS) A.left A.hom
  let F' := (phComparisonMorphism A (fppfTopology B S hS)).inverseImage.obj G
  have hF' := isCartesianOnSections_phComparison_inverseImage (A := A) (fppfTopology B S hS) hX hG
  obtain ⟨H, ⟨e⟩⟩ := SimplicialOver.mem_essImage_augmentationInverseImage_of_isCartesianOnSections
    A.left A.hom (fppfPretopology B S hS) (isHypercoveringAugmentation_of_isFppfHypercovering hA)
    (fppfPretopology_toGrothendieck B S hS) F' hF'
  let a₀ : A.left.obj (op ⦋0⦌) ⟶ A.right := SimplicialOver.augmentationApp A.left A.hom (op ⦋0⦌)
  have : (SimplicialOver.augmentationFibre A.left A.hom (op ⦋0⦌)).IsContinuous
      ((fppfTopology B S hS).over (A.left.obj (op ⦋0⦌))) ((fppfTopology B S hS).over A.right) :=
    inferInstanceAs ((Over.map a₀).IsContinuous _ _)
  let eRestr : ((Over.map a₀).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (u + 1))
      ((fppfTopology B S hS).over (A.left.obj (op ⦋0⦌))) ((fppfTopology B S hS).over A.right)).obj
        H ≅ (phRestrict A (fppfTopology B S hS) (op ⦋0⦌)).obj F' :=
    (Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuousComp' (eqToIso
        (SimplicialOver.ι_comp_augmentationFunctor A.left A.hom (op ⦋0⦌))) (Type (u + 1))
        ((fppfTopology B S hS).over (A.left.obj (op ⦋0⦌)))
        (SimplicialOver.totalTopology (fppfTopology B S hS) A.left)
        ((fppfTopology B S hS).over A.right)).symm.app H ≪≫
      (phRestrict A (fppfTopology B S hS) (op ⦋0⦌)).mapIso
        ((SimplicialOver.augmentationInverseImageIso A.left A.hom
          (fppfTopology B S hS)).symm.app H ≪≫ e)
  have h₀ := (mem_essImage_phRestrict_inverseImage (fppfTopology B S hS) (op ⦋0⦌) G).ofIso
    eRestr.symm
  obtain ⟨H', ⟨e'⟩⟩ := mem_essImage_fppfComparison_of_overMap a₀ hA.map_zero h₀
  exact ⟨H', ⟨hffh.preimageIso
    ((phComparisonSquareInverseImageIso A (fppfTopology B S hS)).app H' ≪≫
      aph.inverseImage.mapIso e' ≪≫ e)⟩⟩

/-- **Inverse images along fppf hypercoverings, sheaves of sets** (the content of Stacks 0DH6).
Let `S` be a scheme, `X` an algebraic space over `S`, `U` a simplicial algebraic space over `S`
and `a : U → X` an augmentation which is an fppf hypercovering of `X`. Then
`a⁻¹ : Sh(X_étale) ⥤ Sh(U_étale)` is fully faithful, its essential image consists exactly of the
cartesian sheaves, and `a_*` is a quasi-inverse: the unit of `a⁻¹ ⊣ a_*` is invertible, and so is
its counit at every cartesian sheaf. Here `a : Sh(U_étale) → Sh(X_étale)` is the morphism of topoi
of Section 0DE7. -/
theorem IsFppfHypercovering.etaleAugmentation_inverseImage_fullyFaithful :
    (etaleAugmentationMorphism A).inverseImage.Full ∧
      (etaleAugmentationMorphism A).inverseImage.Faithful ∧
      (∀ G, (etaleAugmentationMorphism A).inverseImage.essImage G ↔
        (etaleSituation A).IsCartesianSheaf G) ∧
      (∀ F, IsIso ((etaleAugmentationMorphism A).adj.unit.app F)) ∧
      (∀ G, (etaleSituation A).IsCartesianSheaf G →
        IsIso ((etaleAugmentationMorphism A).adj.counit.app G)) := by
  have hff := hA.fullyFaithfulEtaleAugmentationInverseImage
  have := hff.full
  have := hff.faithful
  have hess : ∀ G, (etaleAugmentationMorphism A).inverseImage.essImage G ↔
      (etaleSituation A).IsCartesianSheaf G := fun G =>
    ⟨fun ⟨K, ⟨e⟩⟩ => SimplicialSiteSituation.isCartesianSheaf_of_iso (etaleSituation A) e
      (isCartesianSheaf_totalMorphismOfTopoi_inverseImage (etaleSituation A) _ _
        (etaleAugmentation A) K),
      fun hG => hA.mem_essImage_etaleAugmentation_inverseImage hG⟩
  have hunit : IsIso (etaleAugmentationMorphism A).adj.unit :=
    Adjunction.unit_isIso_of_L_fully_faithful _
  refine ⟨hff.full, hff.faithful, hess, fun F => inferInstance, fun G hG => ?_⟩
  exact ((etaleAugmentationMorphism A).adj.isIso_counit_app_iff_mem_essImage).2 ((hess G).2 hG)

/-- **Inverse images along fppf hypercoverings, sheaves of abelian groups** (the content of
Stacks 0DH6). For an fppf hypercovering `a : U → X`, the inverse image
`a⁻¹ : Ab(X_étale) ⥤ Ab(U_étale)` is fully faithful, its essential image consists exactly of the
cartesian abelian sheaves, and the abelian direct image `a_*` is a quasi-inverse: the unit of
`a⁻¹ ⊣ a_*` is invertible, and so is its counit at every cartesian abelian sheaf. -/
theorem IsFppfHypercovering.etaleAugmentation_abelianInverseImage_fullyFaithful :
    (Sites.abelianInverseImage (etaleAugmentationMorphism A)).Full ∧
      (Sites.abelianInverseImage (etaleAugmentationMorphism A)).Faithful ∧
      (∀ G, (Sites.abelianInverseImage (etaleAugmentationMorphism A)).essImage G ↔
        (etaleSituation A).IsCartesianAbSheaf G) ∧
      (∀ F, IsIso ((abelianInverseImageAdjPushforward
        (etaleSimplicialSite A).totalTopology (etaleAugmentationMorphism A)).unit.app F)) ∧
      (∀ G, (etaleSituation A).IsCartesianAbSheaf G →
        IsIso ((abelianInverseImageAdjPushforward
          (etaleSimplicialSite A).totalTopology (etaleAugmentationMorphism A)).counit.app G)) := by
  obtain ⟨-, -, -, hunit, hcounit⟩ := hA.etaleAugmentation_inverseImage_fullyFaithful
  let JU := (etaleSimplicialSite A).totalTopology
  let adj := abelianInverseImageAdjPushforward JU (etaleAugmentationMorphism A)
  have hunitAb : ∀ F, IsIso (adj.unit.app F) := by
    intro F
    refine isIso_of_isIso_forget_map _ ?_
    rw [abelianInverseImageAdjPushforward_unit_forget JU (etaleAugmentationMorphism A) F]
    exact hunit _
  have hcounitAb : ∀ G, (etaleSituation A).IsCartesianAbSheaf G → IsIso (adj.counit.app G) := by
    intro G hG
    refine isIso_of_isIso_forget_map _ ?_
    rw [abelianInverseImageAdjPushforward_counit_forget JU (etaleAugmentationMorphism A) G]
    exact hcounit _ hG
  have : IsIso adj.unit := NatIso.isIso_of_isIso_app _
  have hff := adj.fullyFaithfulLOfIsIsoUnit
  refine ⟨hff.full, hff.faithful, fun G => ⟨fun ⟨K, ⟨e⟩⟩ => ?_, fun hG => ?_⟩, hunitAb,
    hcounitAb⟩
  · exact SimplicialSiteSituation.isCartesianSheaf_of_iso (etaleSituation A)
      ((sheafCompose JU (forget AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})).mapIso e)
      (isCartesianAbSheaf_totalInverseImageAb (etaleSituation A) _ _ (etaleAugmentation A) K)
  · have := hcounitAb G hG
    exact ⟨_, ⟨asIso (adj.counit.app G)⟩⟩

/-- **Every cartesian abelian sheaf on `U_étale` is `a⁻¹` of an abelian sheaf on `X_étale`**, for
an fppf hypercovering `a : U → X` (the content of Stacks 0DH6). -/
theorem IsFppfHypercovering.mem_essImage_totalInverseImageAb
    (G : Sheaf (etaleSituation A).totalTopology AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1})
    (hG : SimplicialSiteSituation.IsCartesianAbSheaf (etaleSituation A) G) :
    (totalInverseImageAb (etaleSituation A) _ _ (etaleAugmentation A)).essImage G :=
  (hA.etaleAugmentation_abelianInverseImage_fullyFaithful.2.2.1 G).2 hG

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

/-! ## Stacks 0DH6 on the small étale site of `X`

Section 0DE7 works with the small étale site `X_étale` of Properties of Spaces, Definition 03ED,
whose objects are schemes étale over `X`, and identifies its topos with that of the spaces-étale
site through the inclusion of Stacks 03G1. The statements registered for Stacks 0DH6 are on
`X_étale` itself: `a⁻¹ : Sh(X_étale) ⥤ Sh(U_étale)` is the inverse of the equivalence
`Sh(X_spaces,étale) ≌ Sh(X_étale)` given by restriction along
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.comparisonFunctor`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.comparisonFunctor_sheafEquivalence`) followed by the inverse image of
the morphism of topoi of Section 0DE7, and the content on the
spaces-étale site is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFppfHypercovering.etaleAugmentation_inverseImage_fullyFaithful` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsFppfHypercovering.etaleAugmentation_abelianInverseImage_fullyFaithful`
above. `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.effectiveFppfDescent` records the flat case of Stacks 0GFW in the
form `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.EffectiveFppfDescent`.
-/

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable (B : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : B.Contains S)

/-- **Effective descent of spaces-étale sheaves along fppf coverings.** Along every morphism of
algebraic spaces over `S` which is surjective, flat and locally of finite presentation, sheaves on
the spaces-étale site of the target are equivalent, through the canonical descent datum, to
descent data for the one-member family. This is the flat case of Stacks 0GFW,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEquivalence_toDescentData_singleton_of_isFlat`, whose input Stacks
0GFV is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isEquivalence_toDescentData_singleton_of_relativelyRepresentable_comp`.
-/
@[sga "4 VIII 9.4" "more general"]
theorem effectiveFppfDescent : EffectiveFppfDescent B S hS :=
  fun _ _ f hsurj hflat hfp =>
    isEquivalence_toDescentData_singleton_of_isFlat B S hS
      (fun π g hrep hcov =>
        isEquivalence_toDescentData_singleton_of_relativelyRepresentable_comp B S hS π g hrep hcov)
      f hsurj hflat hfp

